From 75f88fa986e1df0496cff83c982aa12fe98ac5c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:06:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add functional wooden door with block states

- Block states: a block JSON can list "properties" (and per-state "variants");
  the registry expands it into one ordinary block ID per combination, named
  e.g. cuboidfever:wooden_door[facing=north,half=lower,open=false]. Chunks,
  saves, palette and lighting are unchanged; the plain name resolves to the
  default state. New helpers: GetBaseName, GetDefaultState, GetState, WithState.
- wooden_door.json: lower/upper halves, 4 facings, open/closed (16 IDs), using
  the wooden_door_{bottom,top}_{f,s} textures (copied into textures/block).
- Door is a 3/16 slab (BlockShapes): closed behind the placing player, open
  swung to their left. Meshed as a box with front/edge textures.
- Player collision, raycast and target outline use the real slab, not a cube.
- Right-click toggles both halves; placing makes a 2-tall door facing the
  player; breaking either half removes both. Door added to the hotbar.
- Tests for state expansion and door geometry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
